    <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--color-ink-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">Beta review draft · Last source audit: 18 October 2026</p>

    <h2>What The Vinyl Drop does</h2>
    <p>The Vinyl Drop is a community marketplace for discovering, listing, buying, selling and trading physical vinyl records. The current application does not take payments or provide escrow. Published listings, their photos, public profile fields and comments may be visible to other visitors.</p>

    <h2>Information handled by the current application</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account and sign-in:</strong> email address, Supabase Auth user ID, authentication state and session tokens. Supabase Auth manages passwords and OAuth credentials; the application does not store plaintext passwords in its application tables.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile:</strong> username, display name, avatar URL, optional website, bio, coarse location and timestamps. Public profile fields may be visible. The intended location granularity is city or neighborhood, not a street address.</li>
      <li><strong>Records and listings:</strong> artist/title/release metadata, label/catalogue details, format, copy condition, price/trade status, description, publication state and relevant timestamps.</li>
      <li><strong>Photos:</strong> processed listing images, storage paths, ordering and alt text. The upload pipeline converts supported images to WebP, resizes large images and strips EXIF metadata. Listing imagery is served from a public-read bucket, so do not upload private or sensitive images.</li>
      <li><strong>Community activity:</strong> comments, favorites and activity events. Comments on visible listings are public. Favorites are intended to remain private; some activity events can appear on community activity surfaces.</li>
      <li><strong>Security/operational information:</strong> bounded application/runtime error information and hosting logs. Provider log retention has not yet been verified.</li>
      <li><strong>Password safety check:</strong> for the app's new-password check, a five-character SHA-1 hash prefix is sent to the Have I Been Pwned range API; the full hash is compared locally. This is an application-path control, not a claim that Supabase's native leaked-password warning is cleared.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Waitlist</h2>
    <p>The source audit did not find a waitlist table or waitlist collection route. This application is not currently collecting waitlist addresses. Do not enable any waitlist collection until its purpose, provider, access, retention and deletion process have been approved separately.</p>

    <h2>Why information is used</h2>
    <p>The current application uses information to sign users in, maintain profiles, manage record listings, display photos and comments, support discovery, operate and secure the service, investigate faults, and check new passwords against a known-breach list.</p>
    <p><strong>Owner/legal approval required:</strong> the lawful basis for each purpose has not yet been approved in this draft.</p>

    <h2>Services that may receive information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase:</strong> authentication, PostgreSQL database and listing-photo storage.</li>
      <li><strong>Render:</strong> web hosting/runtime and platform logs.</li>
      <li><strong>Discogs and/or MusicBrainz:</strong> catalog searches/lookups when those features are used.</li>
      <li><strong>Have I Been Pwned:</strong> the password range check described above.</li>
      <li><strong>Auth/email providers:</strong> sign-in verification, password recovery and Google OAuth flows.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The deployed provider settings, data-processing terms, regions, international transfers and provider retention defaults still need review. This draft does not make claims about them.</p>

    <h2>Sign-in cookies</h2>
    <p>The source currently sets essential authentication/session cookies: <code>sb-access-token</code> (session expiry, normally one hour if no expiry is returned), <code>sb-refresh-token</code> (configured for up to 30 days), <code>sb-recovery-mode</code> (15 minutes) and temporary Supabase PKCE/auth-flow values (up to 10 minutes). These are HTTP-only, use SameSite=Lax, and follow the application's environment-specific Secure-cookie policy.</p>
    <p>No analytics or advertising tracker was identified in the tracked application source/package manifest during the 18 October 2026 source audit. Deployed browser/network behavior and third-party resource requests have not yet been verified, so this is not a final no-tracking claim. The owner must decide whether a separate cookie notice is needed after that check.</p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p><strong>Not approved yet.</strong> The repository has some timestamps, foreign-key cascades, listing-photo cleanup and cookie expiries, but no complete, owner-approved retention schedule for accounts/profiles, listings/comments, favorites/activity, catalog metadata, Storage objects, diagnostics or provider logs. Archived content is not the same as deleted content. The application does not currently provide self-service account export or full account deletion.</p>
    <p>Before this notice is approved, the owner must define what starts deletion for each data category, what is removed, what may be retained for security/operational reasons, and which provider/back-up retention cannot be controlled directly.</p>

    <h2>Questions, access, correction or deletion requests</h2>
    <p>The existing Contact page currently lists <a href="mailto:yepyouknowhim@gmail.com">yepyouknowhim@gmail.com</a>. You may use it to contact the project about a privacy question or request. The responsible human, identity-verification process, request log, response procedure and deletion steps still need an owner-approved runbook. The app does not currently offer self-service export or deletion.</p>

    <h2>Responsible operator</h2>
    <p><strong>Required before approval:</strong> the responsible operator's legal name and public address have not been verified from repository source. This page must not be approved until the owner confirms the correct identity and the information that should be published.</p>

